# <%= current_page.data.title %>

**A successful, supported in-place upgrade retains existing databases and their
data on the same server**, keeping its name and connection endpoint. All databases
on the server move to the target engine version.

## Changing the API version

Use `v20250801`, as shown on
[line 1 of Toffee's server manifest](https://github.com/hmcts/sds-flux-config/blob/master/apps/toffee/sbox/aso/toffee-postgres.yaml#L1):

```yaml
apiVersion: dbforpostgresql.azure.com/v20250801
```

Confirm ASO supports the new API and coordinate matching shared-resource and
patch APIs to avoid Kustomize failures. Unrelated ASO APIs need no change.
Changing the API alone does not upgrade the engine.

## Select a version

Check the shared manifest in
[SDS](https://github.com/hmcts/sds-flux-config/blob/master/apps/azureserviceoperator-system/resources/flexibleserver-postgres.yaml)
or [CNP](https://github.com/hmcts/cnp-flux-config/blob/master/apps/azureserviceoperator-system/resources/flexibleserver-postgres.yaml)
for the configured default. Override it in the team server patch using
`spec.version`, for example `"16"` to retain 16 or `"17"` to select 17.
Keep other settings unchanged; never select a lower version to downgrade a server.


## Prepare and verify an upgrade

Follow Microsoft's [upgrade guidance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/postgresql/flexible-server/concepts-major-version-upgrade):
Test in non-production using a confirmed ASO upgrade method. Afterwards, verify your database version, data and application connectivity.

## Toffee example

See [Toffee's upgrade-test PR #9060](https://github.com/hmcts/sds-flux-config/pull/9060/files),
which changes the existing test server's `spec.version` from `"14"` to `"17"`.
Toffee already used `v20250801`, so that PR contains no API change.
This shows the Git change, not confirmed upgrade success; deployed version and
data-preservation checks are still needed.
